diff --git a/docs/reference/config.rst b/docs/reference/config.rst
index 85a03364..1d4d0294 100644
--- a/docs/reference/config.rst
+++ b/docs/reference/config.rst
@@ -2349,6 +2349,23 @@ separators:
 Multiple dots can be escaped in the same key: ``-x 'some\.dotted\.name.key=val'``. A backslash not followed by a dot
 passes through literally.
 
+Substitutions inside an override
+================================
+
+.. versionadded:: 4.61
+
+An override value goes through the same substitution pass as a value in the configuration file, so references such as
+``{posargs}``, ``{posargs:default}``, ``{env:VAR}`` and ``{env_name}`` are resolved before the value is used. For
+example, the following runs ``pytest -k slow``, because ``{posargs:tests}`` falls back to ``tests`` only when no
+positional arguments are given:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   tox -x env_run_base.commands='pytest {posargs:tests}' -e py -- -k slow
+
+Overrides use the INI spelling of a substitution even in a TOML project, so write ``{env:VAR}`` rather than the TOML
+form when overriding from the command line.
+
 ***********
  TOML only
 ***********
